  "sent_to_model": "right so i moved flat a few weeks ago and used Kilbarrack Van Co, dessie who runs it drinks in the venue and he's after asking me twice now to leave him a google review. which is grand they were mostly great. but they were late and the lamp got chipped and i dont want to lie about that either cos people read these to decide. can u write one thats fair, like honest but not dropping him in it. he will 100% read it and so will half the bar lol. heres what happened\n\n- moved sat 17 oct, phibsborough to drumcondra, 2 bed flat but mostly my stuff, 4th floor walkup no lift at the new place\n- quote was 340 for up to 4 hrs, 2 lads + the van, took about 3 and a half\n- dessie knocked 40 off after cos of the lateness, didnt even ask him to\n- booked through their website, deposit 50 by revolut\n- meant to arrive 9, came at half 10, did text at 8:40 saying previous job overran, i was sat on boxes with a cold coffee\n- the couch wouldnt go round the turn on the 3rd floor, young lad (Kev?) took the legs off with an allen key from his pocket and it went straight in\n- brass floor lamp base got chipped, they wrapped everything else in blankets but not that, my nannys lamp so a bit gutted\n- they put the bed back together for me without being asked, and took away the flat pack shelf i didnt want\n- would use again honestly, best value i found, other quotes were 450+\n- lateness wasnt the end of the world but if ur on a tight handover with a landlord it would be\n- wrap the lamps lads\n- 4 stars not 5, think thats fair\n- want it to be useful to someone who is moving, not just a thank you to dessie\n\n(About me: bartender at a music venue, 31, Dublin, Ireland. Length: it should come to roughly 400-800 words.)",
